.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-TEST-NATIVE-INIT 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-test-native-init
.Nd consume experimental sys-init artifacts in an isolated Aether test workspace
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3
.Ar tests/native-init.py
.br
.Fl Fl producer Ar directory
.br
.Fl Fl summary-pin Ar digest
.br
.Fl Fl work Ar directory
.br
.Op Fl Fl init-large | Fl Fl init-composed
.Op Fl Fl deps Ar directory
.br
.Op Fl Fl service-worker Ar directory
.br
.Op Fl Fl service-worker-pin Ar digest
.Nm python3
.Ar tests/native-init.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3
.Ar tests/native-init.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This source-checkout developer command performs actual kernel builds and
native
QEMU smoke tests.
It is not an installed operator command, a host-only model
check or permission to test arbitrary images.
Use trusted, independently reviewed
inputs and tools matching the selected retained experiment.
The command copies inputs to a new workspace and builds there rather than in
the original kernel tree.
Existing workspace paths are rejected.
No root privileges, host service installation or physical target access is
needed.
.Pp
Use Python 3.12 or newer with tarfile's data extraction filter, Rust 1.98.0
with
x86_64-unknown-none, and the producer-compatible Zig/QEMU toolchain and boot
inputs.
All tools/dependencies must be provisioned before offline execution.
The producer summary pins the source archive and passing init report, which
pins the positive envelope.
Profile magic, sizes, reserved fields and both
helper ELF payloads must match.
The copied inputs are validated again before
extracting the producer archive with the data filter; archived source hashes
are checked against the summary.
An optional service worker must have a matching
passing receipt, artifact hash and safe relative input hashes.
.Pp
The default remains AENIN001/ABI 6 with a 4096-byte supervisor bound.
The explicit large profile uses AENIN002/ABI 15 and an 8192-byte bound, with
archived pinned boot dependencies.
The mutually exclusive composed profile uses AENIN003/ABI 16, a 16384-byte
code bound and the unchanged 4096-byte stack. Its consumer-owned intake summary
binds the original producer archive/report/envelope and packet provenance.
It includes generated-dependent Terminal, issued-reclaim and Cleaned probes.
The three Cleaned and four complete-pair cases explicitly add fat LTO and one
codegen unit to fit the
unchanged code limit; other cases retain their prior compiler options.
Commands in results.json record these per-case options.
The base build_profile names retained-sampling-v1; it is not a claim that all
cases use identical compiler flags.
The compiler profile remains
retained-sampling-v1, size optimization and a remapped source path.
The fixed case set depends on profile and optional service-worker selection;
there is no individual-case filter.
Expected panic/receipt contexts are source
oracles, not arbitrary user-configurable success strings.
The runner verifies copied dependencies and logs Rust, Zig and QEMU versions.
Kernel builds disable SMP.
Guest success, owner-close and semantic rejection
checks apply to the selected profile only.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl producer Ar directory
Reviewed producer bundle with summary.json, source archive and init artifacts.
.It Fl Fl summary-pin Ar digest
Externally retained SHA-256 of the producer summary.
.It Fl Fl work Ar directory
New private workspace; must not already exist.
.It Fl Fl init-large
Select ABI 15 explicitly.
The producer must match; this does not convert ABI 6.
.It Fl Fl init-composed
Select ABI 16 explicitly using a reviewed sys-init-init-composed-intake-v1
summary. It cannot be combined with --init-large.
.It Fl Fl deps Ar directory
Required for ABI 6, copied as boot dependencies.
Forbidden with --init-large or --init-composed,
which consumes archived dependencies instead.
.It Fl Fl service-worker Ar directory
Optional sys-init service-worker build with evidence.json and
service-worker.elf.
Enables the corresponding additional fixed cases after receipt validation.
.It Fl Fl service-worker-pin Ar digest
Required by validation when a service-worker directory is supplied.
Without that directory, this option alone is ignored by current code.
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without creating a workspace or launching tools.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the harness-command version and exit, not a published release version.
.El
.Pp
Relative input/work paths are resolved from the caller's working directory.
Do not place the new workspace inside any input tree: the harness copies those
trees and does not uniformly enforce that separation.
Reserve a private path
outside producer/SDK/dependency directories and preserve failed workspaces.
.Sh OUTPUT AND FILES
Per-case [OK] progress goes to standard error; successful completion prints
JSON with result and report path. results.json uses sys-init-native-init-v1
and
records selected native/build profiles, producer/worker identities, commands,
case expectations and artifact hashes. sources.json fingerprints copied
inputs,
producer and client sources. inputs/, sys-init/, Aether/, cases/ and command
logs
remain in the workspace.
Exceptions in the case-run section save failure or
interrupted status and re-raise; setup failures can precede a report.
.Pp
A running, missing, incomplete or failed report is not passing evidence.
Do not erase unsuccessful attempts or substitute a previous passing report for
current inputs.
A passing guest run applies only to its selected frozen profile.
.Sh LIMITS AND ENVIRONMENT
The host environment selects tools through PATH; Python and producer smoke
scripts can inherit other host settings.
There is no downloader or hosted CI
setup in this command.
A copy/hash record alone is not a live sandbox guarantee.
Tool commands have 180-second wait deadlines and owned sessions.
Timeout/interruption cleanup kills the owned trusted, non-detaching process
group.
Logs stream to files without a separate size cap.
Copying and hashing are outside
these per-command deadlines; there is no overall suite deadline.
Guest smoke
watchdogs are separate producer-owned behavior, not a substitute for host
bounds.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
All selected cases completed successfully, or a supported help/version query.
.It 1
An ordinary Python exception or explicit semantic/build rejection.
Other interpreter/signal termination statuses are possible.
.It 64
Invalid usage or incompatible required option combinations.
.It 130
An uncaught KeyboardInterrupt under ordinary Python invocation; if caught by
the case-run section, the retained report is marked interrupted.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the repository root, inspect usage without starting a guest:
.Bd -literal -offset left
python3 tests/native-init.py --help
.Ed
.Pp
A full invocation below starts real builds/QEMU.
First set the quoted shell
variables from an independently reviewed handoff; they are placeholders, not
harness environment settings.
WORK must name a new private directory outside
all input trees.
No root privileges are required.
.Bd -literal -offset left
python3 tests/native-init.py \e
  --producer "$PRODUCER" --summary-pin "$SUMMARY_PIN" \e
  --deps "$DEPS" --work "$WORK"
.Ed
.Pp
Expect all selected cases, exit zero and the documented outputs on success.
Retain the entire workspace on failure; do not rerun into an existing
workspace.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository guides: docs/NATIVE-COVERAGE.md, docs/LIFECYCLE-V1.md,
docs/NATIVE-SUPERVISION.md, docs/NATIVE-IO.md, docs/NATIVE-ADAPTER.md
and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
Exact retained decisions define compatible
producer inputs and test oracles; manuals do not replace those contracts.
.Sh CAVEATS
Independent technical/reader review and installed-target manual lookup remain
pending.
The native init profiles are experiments, not production POSIX init.
